{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MF-005","evidence":[{"kind":"note","ref":"N1","page":1,"quote":"HEAT TREATMENT :-\n1) TO BE TOUGHENED UPTO 28-32 HRC.\n2) RETAPPING TO BE DONE AFTER SURFACE TREATMENT AT SUPPLIER END.( IF APPLICABLE )"}],"comment":"The note specifies the hardness (28-32 HRC) but does not state at which manufacturing stage the heat treatment applies (e.g., before or after machining, before surface treatment). Without a defined sequence the shop cannot plan operations correctly and risks distorting finished features or plating over unhardened material. The designer should add the process stage to N1, for example 'TO BE TOUGHENED UPTO 28-32 HRC BEFORE FINAL MACHINING AND SURFACE TREATMENT.'."
  ,
  "recommended_correction":"Update note N1 to explicitly state when the heat treatment is to be performed relative to machining and surface treatment."}]}
